    "catalysts": [],
    "industrial_process_notes": "First discovered in 1898 by Alfred Einhorn but abandoned for 30 years. Hermann Schnell (Bayer, Uerdingen) patented the first linear polycarbonate in 1953; Daniel Fox (General Electric) independently synthesized a branched variant around the same time. Bayer commercialized Makrolon in 1958; GE launched Lexan in 1960. ~1 billion kg produced annually via the phosgene route.",
    "synthesis_scheme_image": null
  },
